Counsel,<br />
<br />
Served today: Respondent's motion for summary disposition, and notice that =
Respondent will seek fees and expenses of $186,300 under the Equal Access t=
o Justice Act if it prevails. The motion is attached.<br />
<br />
The motion rests on the Division's own production. In 2011 the Commission's=
 staff examined this exact practice at this exact firm. The complete examin=
ation file the Division produced consists of a summary record showing dispo=
sition "closed - no further action" and a closing letter stating that the s=
taff has closed the examination and will take no further action. There is n=
o deficiency letter in the production. There is no correspondence. There is=
 nothing requiring my client to do anything, because nothing was required o=
f my client.<br />
<br />
Marchwood disclosed the arrangement, the staff examined it, and the staff c=
losed. My client then continued a practice the Commission's own examiners h=
ad reviewed and passed. The Division now seeks $4,300,000 from a firm for d=
oing what the agency told it, in writing, it was free to do.<br />
<br />
If the Division has a document showing that something was in fact required =
of Marchwood in 2011, produce it. If it does not, this proceeding is not su=
bstantially justified and should be dismissed.<br />
<br />
J. Roland Ballentine<br />
Ballentine Roe LLP
